   regularity and order pattern in time series},
Journal = {GEOMAGNETISM AND AERONOMY},
Year = {2013},
Volume = {53},
Number = {8},
Pages = {922-926},
Month = {DEC},
Abstract = {The several competing reconstructions of Northern Hemisphere temperature
   variability exists with partly conflicting evidence. Here we considered
   a specific problem of choosing ``the best{''} reconstruction, in a frame
   of assumptions, that they are produced by smooth dynamical system as
   well as instrumental time series. Using some sophisticated measures of
   similarity, we could not match to all existing hemispheric paleoclimate
   reconstructions with hypothesis about any deterministic system which can
   produced its as typical projection of their trajectories. The results
   cast doubt on the conventional techniques frequently used to reconstruct
   past climate variability.},
