Organization = {IEEE; IEEE Geosci \& Remote Sensing Soc; NASA; NOAA; USN Off Res; Japan
   Aerosp Explorat Agcy; Natl Polar orbiting Operat Environm Satellite
   Syst; Ball Aerosp \& Technologies Corp; Int Union Radio Sci; Elect \&
   Telecommun Res Inst; Korea Sci \& Engn Fdn; Korea Natl Tourism Org;
   Korea Telecommun},
Abstract = {According to the regional climatic model and tendency, the long-term
   climatic change, which presents not only the climatic change, but also
   the regional climatic change, is discussed. The glacial scale is a very
   important climatic indicator, which is sensitive to temperature and
   precipitation, and provides a foundation for the comparison of the
   modern and various glaciers in Bodui district. The declination value of
   ELA and the relevant climatic change are estimated. The results of 3
   glaciers on Boduizangbo show that both modern ELA and former ELAs
   decrease from south to north, due to the northwards monsoon and the
   declining precipitation. The value of ELA in LGM Is about 300-600m. If
   the precipitation remains constant, the summer average temperature in
   LGM declines by 3.7-6 K.},
